<!-- CONTEXT: THE COMBAT LOOP -->
<section class="oop-section">
    <div class="oop-section-header">
        <div class="oop-section-icon">
            <i class="fa-solid fa-arrows-spin"></i>
        </div>
        <h2 class="oop-section-title">How It Works: The Combat Loop</h2>
    </div>
    
    <div class="info-content">
        <p>You are implementing the logic for <strong>your turn</strong>. The Engine handles the rest of the battle loop:</p>
        <div class="code-block" style="background: #f1f3f5; padding: 1rem; border-radius: 8px; font-family: monospace; color: #333;">
            <p style="margin: 0;"><strong>WHILE</strong> (Everyone is alive):</p>
            <p style="margin: 0; padding-left: 1rem;">1. Engine asks YOU: choose_action()</p>
            <p style="margin: 0; padding-left: 1rem;">2. Engine asks ENEMY: choose_action()</p>
            <p style="margin: 0; padding-left: 1rem;">3. Engine calculates speed & order</p>
            <p style="margin: 0; padding-left: 1rem;">4. <strong>ATTACKER:</strong> compute_damage() is called</p>
            <p style="margin: 0; padding-left: 1rem;">5. Engine subtracts HP and prints results</p>
        </div>
        <p style="margin-top: 1rem;">The Engine takes care of the loop, the printing, and the enemy AI. You just need to say <strong>what you do</strong> and <strong>how hard you hit</strong>.</p>
    </div>
</section>

<!-- STRUCTURE GUIDE -->
<section class="oop-section">
    <div class="oop-section-header">
        <div class="oop-section-icon">
            <i class="fa-solid fa-code"></i>
        </div>
        <h2 class="oop-section-title">Structure Guide</h2>
    </div>
    
    <p class="section-intro">Add these two methods to your Player class.</p>
    
    <!-- 1. choose_action -->
    <details class="skeleton-block" open>
        <summary class="skeleton-summary">
            <span class="skeleton-step">1</span>
            <span class="skeleton-title">choose_action (Selection Hook)</span>
            <i class="fa-solid fa-chevron-down skeleton-chevron"></i>
        </summary>
        <div class="skeleton-content">
            <div class="skeleton-line code">METHOD choose_action(options_list) → integer:</div>
            <div class="skeleton-desc">
                <strong>Purpose:</strong> Let the player pick a combat move.<br>
                <strong>Logic:</strong> This works exactly like <code>respond_to_npc</code>!
                <ul>
                    <li>The engine already displays the numbered options</li>
                    <li>Ask the user for input</li>
                    <li>Validate it's a number and in range</li>
                    <li>Return the 0-based index</li>
                </ul>
            </div>
        </div>
    </details>
    
    <!-- 2. compute_damage -->
    <details class="skeleton-block">
        <summary class="skeleton-summary">
            <span class="skeleton-step">2</span>
            <span class="skeleton-title">compute_damage (Calculation Hook)</span>
            <i class="fa-solid fa-chevron-down skeleton-chevron"></i>
        </summary>
        <div class="skeleton-content">
            <div class="skeleton-line code">METHOD compute_damage(base_damage, armour) → integer:</div>
            <div class="skeleton-desc">
                <strong>Requirement:</strong> Calculate damage: <code>Damage = Base - Armour</code><br>
                <strong>Constraint:</strong> Damage cannot be negative! Use <code>max()</code> function.
                <div class="skeleton-line code" style="margin-top: 0.5rem;">damage = base_damage - armour</div>
                <div class="skeleton-line code">return MAX(0, damage)</div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </details>
</section>

